{"agent_id":"pp3g-Za1m-continuation-of-observer-v1-build-on-issue-460-prior","agent_seq":8,"timestamp":"2026-08-25T00:34:41.850160480Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"1119c189-2781-4d21-bbc7-53157a03d0c2","comment_uuid":"d167da66-0cdb-44d9-b702-221ab879e5b1","author":"pp3g-Za1m-continuation-of-observer-v1-build-on-issue-460-prior","content":"Result: [RESULT][BUILDER] Observer v1 CONTINUATION complete - F4+F5+F6 landed on feature/pp3g-Za1m-continuation-of-observer-v1-build-on-issue-460-prior (commits 2b393473, 7dac3de6, 739025bd), suite 67/67 -> 98/98 green, verified on the committed tree.\n\nF4 DUAL-STORE BACKUP (data-retention.md): wave-level pass, interval-gated OBSERVER_BACKUP_INTERVAL_MINS=1440 default (stores are 2.6+2.9GB live-verified; per-cycle would churn). (a) sqlite3 .backup hot copy of BOTH stores (session-union.py discovery: main:opencode.db + fork:opencode-fork-pp3g.db, env-overridable) with PRAGMA integrity_check + sha256, generations capped KEEP=1; (b) incremental export reads THE SNAPSHOT COPY via immutable URI (zero live-DB load), discovers session/session_v2 at runtime, gzip JSONL under <archive>/exports/<date>/ + uncompressed index keyed (store,session_id) under <archive>/index/, per-(store,table) time_updated watermark advances ONLY after GREEN read-back; (c) rclone sync only when OBSERVER_RCLONE_REMOTE resolves in listremotes, else explicit PENDING line in sync-pending.log naming the unconfigured remote (graceful local mode; secrets doctrine #462 respected - no tokens requested); (d) destination-side read-back (decompress+rowcount+sha256; rclone cat for remote index) appending GREEN/RED lines to verification.log; prune-gate REPORT ONLY (operator-manual deletion v1 per policy) - sessions older than PRUNE_AGE_DAYS listed eligible only when GREEN-covered.\n\nF5 ADMISSION-POLICY ABSORPTION: config-driven checks over tracked-agent KICKOFF.md - model-valid vs LIVE catalog (opencode models <provider>, TTL 1800s, OBSERVER_MODELS_CMD template overridable for tests), issue-exists (issue show rc), issue-claimed (locks check parse), estimate-declared (regex); every check -> admission-check event in events.jsonl audit trail; deduped alerts to flag issue until failure fingerprint changes; NO new plugin files (#448/#445 family absorbed).\n\nF6 WAVE-ANOMALY: all-agents-vanish transition (every active/parked agent absent from scan simultaneously, no terminal verdicts, no Observer cleanup) emits platform-restart signature alert to flag issue + wave-anomaly event; scan-based tracking so re-arm survives phase degradation; deduped per episode; normal wind-down never triggers.\n\nBUGS CAUGHT BY NEW TESTS (both fixed): [1] second-resolution export stamps let a same-second pass silently OVERWRITE an earlier artifact (data loss) - stamps now carry microseconds; [2] bash ${VAR:-word} leaks an extra } into the SET-var value when word ends in a brace - corrupted {provider} placeholder; default now single-quoted. Also hardened: test harness disables backup pass by default (fresh state dirs would hot-copy real stores every cycle) after observing exactly that during an aborted run.\n\nWHY: completes the consolidated dispatch spec M2 remaining items exactly as scoped; WHAT: evidence = 98/98 suite incl. T15 fixture-store backup tests (hot copy, GREEN verify, index, pending flag, prune gate, incrementality single-row delta, generation cap), T16 admission checks incl. live issue-exists/claimed against #460, T17 anomaly fire/dedup/re-arm/refire; plus one live end-to-end pass against the real stores (2032 rows exported GREEN, watermark held on forced second pass, 1-row delta picked up). HOW CERTAIN: evidence-based for everything above. WHAT-NOT-TESTED: real rclone remote sync (no remote wired yet - negative gate tested, positive path awaits orchestrator wiring); RED verification branch not fault-injected (code path inspected only); non-dry-run mutations end-to-end (orchestrator verifies at shakedown n=1); long-duration loop behavior with real interval gating.","created_at":"2026-08-25T00:34:41.840908474Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:O05dKMjpFuMdmfsh5ehsbZ68nszFiLwrSUp8bti/X7I","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgzsl5kzNHs0st6frW0D8e72V6iveTqRAm54s6zUQr8qQAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABADYINOmJvYurY7+JEMxWN5LbnES8EFS2T4yaC1p64aoYP3krS+TrdhECtg21xBbcX90o027N7D/8NNtz5WztHBQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:O05dKMjpFuMdmfsh5ehsbZ68nszFiLwrSUp8bti/X7I","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgzsl5kzNHs0st6frW0D8e72V6iveTqRAm54s6zUQr8qQAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNy9EoUmaKGM7JnTLLVunanyLepaTHMo5S15SXsB4I6IvJO83g7hEpNk9yDsITNs923DEyq0IeDmKwpjDrT5AQc="}
